# Coding Standards and Best Practices

## Core Principles

- Follow WordPress coding standards for PHP development
- Implement mobile-first responsive design
- Use test-driven development (TDD) approach
- Maintain comprehensive documentation
- Ensure security best practices
- Optimize for performance
- Follow SOLID principles

## Code Organization

### File Structure
- Break large files into smaller modules (<100 lines)
- Use descriptive file names following UcF conventions
- Organize by feature or domain rather than type
- Maintain clear separation of concerns
- Implement modular architecture

### Naming Conventions
- Variables: camelCase
- Classes: PascalCase
- Constants: UPPER_SNAKE_CASE
- Functions: snake_case (WordPress standard)
- Files: kebab-case
- Follow UcF naming pattern: `ucf-[department].[function]-[description]-[date].[extension]`

## Development Patterns

### WordPress Development
- Use proper hook naming conventions
- Implement nonce verification
- Sanitize inputs and escape outputs
- Use prepared statements for queries
- Follow WordPress.org plugin guidelines
- Implement proper error handling

### JavaScript Development
- Use ES6+ features appropriately
- Implement proper error handling
- Follow async/await patterns
- Maintain consistent event handling
- Implement proper state management
- Use TypeScript where appropriate

### CSS/SCSS Development
- Follow BEM methodology
- Implement mobile-first approach
- Use logical property ordering
- Maintain consistent naming
- Optimize for performance
- Follow accessibility guidelines

## Security Standards

### Input Validation
- Validate all user inputs
- Implement proper sanitization
- Use prepared statements
- Verify nonce tokens
- Check user capabilities
- Implement rate limiting

### Output Escaping
- Escape all output appropriately
- Use context-specific escaping
- Implement XSS prevention
- Follow OWASP guidelines
- Document security measures

## Performance Optimization

### Code Level
- Use efficient algorithms
- Implement proper caching
- Optimize database queries
- Minimize DOM manipulation
- Use appropriate data structures
- Implement lazy loading

### Asset Management
- Optimize images and media
- Implement proper caching
- Use asset versioning
- Minimize HTTP requests
- Follow loading best practices

## Documentation Requirements

### Code Documentation
- Use PHPDoc standards
- Document all functions
- Explain complex logic
- Include usage examples
- Document security considerations
- Maintain changelog

### API Documentation
- Document all endpoints
- Include request/response examples
- Document authentication requirements
- Include error responses
- Maintain versioning information

## Testing Standards

### Unit Testing
- Write comprehensive tests
- Follow AAA pattern
- Implement proper mocking
- Test edge cases
- Maintain high coverage
- Document test cases

### Integration Testing
- Test cross-component functionality
- Verify system integration
- Test error handling
- Validate security measures
- Document test scenarios

## Version Control

### Git Practices
- Use feature branches
- Write clear commit messages
- Follow conventional commits
- Implement proper PR process
- Maintain clean history
- Document significant changes

### Branch Strategy
- main: Production code
- develop: Development branch
- feature/*: Feature branches
- bugfix/*: Bug fix branches
- release/*: Release branches

## Error Handling

### Logging
- Implement comprehensive logging
- Use appropriate log levels
- Include context information
- Follow logging standards
- Maintain log rotation
- Document logging patterns

### Error Recovery
- Implement graceful degradation
- Provide user feedback
- Log error details
- Implement retry mechanisms
- Document recovery procedures

## Accessibility Standards

### WCAG Compliance
- Follow WCAG 2.1 guidelines
- Implement proper ARIA roles
- Maintain keyboard navigation
- Provide alternative text
- Test with screen readers
- Document accessibility features

## Mobile Optimization

### Responsive Design
- Implement mobile-first approach
- Use proper breakpoints
- Optimize for touch interfaces
- Test across devices
- Document responsive patterns

## Cross-Platform Compatibility

### Browser Support
- Test across major browsers
- Implement graceful degradation
- Document browser requirements
- Test responsive behavior
- Maintain compatibility list

### Platform Testing
- Test on major platforms
- Verify mobile compatibility
